``` 

Janet's ducks lay 16 eggs each day. She uses 3 eggs for breakfast every morning and 4 eggs to bake muffins for her friends each day. 

First, calculate the total number of eggs used daily:
$$
3 \text{ (eggs for breakfast)} + 4 \text{ (eggs for muffins)} = 7 \text{ eggs}
$$

Next, determine the number of eggs remaining after using 7 eggs:
$$
16 \text{ (total eggs)} - 7 \text{ (eggs used)} = 9 \text{ eggs}
$$

Janet sells each remaining egg at $2. Therefore, the total amount she makes daily from selling the eggs is:
$$
9 \text{ eggs} \times 2 \text{ dollars per egg} = 18 \text{ dollars}
$$

The final answer is:
$$
\boxed{18}
$$
