**Step 1: Calculate the total number of pieces**

Grandma Jones baked 5 pies, and each pie was cut into 8 pieces. Therefore, the total number of pieces is:

$$
5 \text{ pies} \times 8 \text{ pieces per pie} = 40 \text{ pieces}
$$

---

**Step 2: Determine the number of pieces taken by the guests**

At the end of the evening, there were 14 pieces remaining. To find how many were taken, subtract the number of remaining pieces from the total:

$$
40 \text{ pieces} - 14 \text{ pieces remaining} = 26 \text{ pieces taken}
$$

---

