Now, the total weight he needs to remove is 15 pounds. So the remaining weight he needs to remove with the toys is 15 minus 7.5. Let me subtract that: 15 - 7.5 equals 7.5 pounds. So the toys have to weigh 7.5 pounds in total.

Each toy is 1/2 pound, so I need to find out how many 1/2 pound items make up 7.5 pounds. To do this, I can divide 7.5 by 1/2. Dividing by a fraction is the same as multiplying by its reciprocal, so 7.5 multiplied by 2. That gives 15. Wait, so 7.5 divided by 0.5 is 15? Let me check that again. 7.5 divided by 0.5. Since 0.5 is half, dividing by half is like doubling. So 7.5 times 2 is 15. Yes, that makes sense. So he needs to remove 15 toys.

