The problem states that Peter spends $7 on a movie ticket and $7 on popcorn each time he goes to the movies. This totals to $7 + $7 = $14 per visit. Peter has a total of $42 for the week. To determine how many times he can go to the movies, we divide his total amount of money by the cost per visit:

$$
\frac{42}{14} = 3
$$

Therefore, Peter can go to the movies **3** times. 

